        {
            "type": "patchouli:text",
            "anchor": "charcoal_pile",
            "text": "After the charcoal pit burns out and stops smoking, you will be left with $(thing)Charcoal piles$(). The charcoal pile contains up to 8 layers of $(thing)Charcoal$(). Dig it with a shovel to obtain the charcoal items. Charcoal piles can be added to or placed with $(item)$(k:key.use)$().$(br2)$(bold)TIP:$() Do not cover your charcoal pit with a dense material like cobblestone, or it may fall and destroy your charcoal when completed."
        },
        {
            "type": "patchouli:text",
            "anchor": "coke_oven",
            "title": "Coke Oven",
            "text": "The $(thing)Coke Oven$() is a multiblock that can automatically convert logs into charcoal and coal into $(item)Coke$() while producing $(thing)Creosote$(). This structure becomes available when you first produce $(l:craftsmanship/bloomery)Wrought Iron$() and it is recommended to make one as soon as possible. Coke ovens are a massive quality of life upgrade for charcoal production, and both coke and creosote will be necessary for progression."
        },
        {
            "type": "patchouli:multiblock",
            "multiblock": {
                "pattern": [
                    [
                        "AAA",
                        "A2A",
                        "AAA"
                    ],
                    [
                        "A1A",
                        "C A",
                        "AAA"
                    ],
                    [
                        "AAA",
                        "A0A",
                        "AAA"
                    ]
                ],
                "mapping": {
                    "0": "gtceu:coke_oven_hatch[facing=down]",
                    "1": "gtceu:coke_oven_hatch[facing=west]",
                    "2": "gtceu:coke_oven_hatch[facing=up]",
                    "A": "gtceu:coke_oven_bricks",
                    "C": "gtceu:coke_oven[facing=north]"
                }
            },
            "text": "An example coke oven with three hatches. Fit for item input, item output, and fluid output.",
            "enable_visualize": true
        },
        {
            "type": "patchouli:text",
            "title": "Coke Oven Tips",
            "text": "$(li)Coke ovens can have up to 4 hatches, replaceing any coke oven brick.$(li)Coke ovens must be hollow in the center.$(li)The coke oven input hatch may get clogged with the output item. To avoid this have an item pipe facing the input hatch with its flow direction set. You can use a hopper or chute to push into that pipe.$(li)Crates are able to hold logs, unlike chests.$(li)Save all your creosote!"
        },
